My friend and I were playing Nethack 3.1 for the PC that was released
"unofficially" on the ftp.uu.net machine.  Although it played well, a
couple of things would kill it.

One which was all but definite was using the exit to shell command in the
game which allows you to temporarily shell out to DOS without quitting the
game.  *CRASH*  This took down the machine and filled the screen with
endless "@" signs.

The other was less tracable, but just seemed to be random failings of the
game with no more that I can describe as collapses of the dungeon.  We'll
try to report backj more on this.  Hopefully, the slew of people playing it
will alert the Nethack Programming team to the programs few flaws and
release the first patchlevel.

Also, the Nethack for Mac "unofficial" was nice but needs a little work. 
The older one worked a little more like a Mac program in some areas,
especially setup.  I'd like to see a real refined interface on this one.

